  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}t-\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2t-3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\pi +2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi +2 & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ \\pi +2 & =\\pi -3(1)+C \\\\ \\pi +2 & =\\pi -3+C \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=2t-3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)+5.$",
